Subject: winewayland: Show frames other processes draw into a window.

Wayland can't put one client's surface inside another client's window, so a Vulkan swapchain one
Wine process creates for a window owned by another gets a wl_surface the compositor never shows.
That is how Chromium/CEF draws in windowed mode: the GPU process presents into the browser
process's child window ("Chrome Legacy Window"). EA app 13.836 (and the Windows Steam client)
stayed an empty window on Wayland; X11 works because winex11 refuses such surfaces and Chromium
falls back to drawing into the foreign X window with GDI.

The drawing process now reads such frames back (GameNative #122 readback in win32u, on by default;
WINE_DISABLE_VULKAN_OPWR=1 turns it off; winex11 still refuses other process surfaces unless
WINE_DISABLE_VULKAN_OPWR=0, so X11 is unchanged), copies them into a section shared with the
window's owner (handle duplicated into the owner once per size) and posts WM_WAYLAND_XPROC_FRAME.
The owner shows them in a subsurface of its toplevel over the window's client area (above the
toplevel's own client surface, empty input region), hides it when the window is hidden and frees
it with the window. One message at a time per window (pending flag), seqlock against tearing.
Swapchains on a process's own windows are not touched.

